Here’s a simple registration page. Save it as `index.html` and open it in a browser. The form is visual only—it doesn’t store or submit registrations yet.

````html name=index.html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Registration</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background: #f2f4f8;
      display: grid;
      min-height: 100vh;
      place-items: center;
      margin: 0;
    }

    form {
      background: white;
      width: min(320px, 85vw);
      padding: 24px;
      border-radius: 8px;
      box-shadow: 0 2px 12px #0002;
    }

    h1 { margin-top: 0; }

    label {
      display: block;
      margin-top: 14px;
    }

    input {
      box-sizing: border-box;
      width: 100%;
      padding: 10px;
      margin-top: 5px;
    }

    button {
      width: 100%;
      padding: 11px;
      margin-top: 20px;
      border: 0;
      border-radius: 4px;
      background: #1769e0;
      color: white;
      cursor: pointer;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <form>
    <h1>Create an account</h1>

    <label for="name">Name</label>
    <input id="name" name="name" type="text" required>

    <label for="email">Email</label>
    <input id="email" name="email" type="email" required>

    <label for="password">Password</label>
    <input id="password" name="password" type="password" required minlength="8">

    <button type="submit">Register</button>
  </form>
</body>
</html>
````
